{:edb/db-before-t 2451 :edb/db-after-t 2452 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535764 50 #inst "2026-10-09T06:46:09.535Z" 13194139535764 true] [17592186133796 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365165 13194139535764 true] [17592186133796 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365172 13194139535764 true] [17592186133797 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365179 13194139535764 true] [17592186133797 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365186 13194139535764 true] [17592186133798 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365193 13194139535764 true] [17592186133982 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535764 true] [17592186133982 1100 "Let $V = R_{1}[t]$, the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $1$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$⟨p(t), q(t)⟩ = p(0)q(0) + p(1)q(1)$,\nfind the orthogonal projection of $p(t) =-3t - 2$ onto the subspace spanned by the polynomial $q(t) = t$." 13194139535764 false] [17592186133982 1100 "Let $V={R}_{1}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $1$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $p(t)=-3t-2$ onto the subspace spanned by the polynomial $q(t)=t.$" 13194139535764 true] [17592186133982 1145 "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{q(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)=\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(-3t-2){|}_{0}\\cdot (t){|}_{0}+(-3t-2){|}_{1}\\cdot (t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 0+(-5)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0-5 \\\\  & =-5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),q(t)⟩ & =q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(t){|}_{0}\\cdot (t){|}_{0}+(t){|}_{1}\\cdot (t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{1}\\cdot t \\\\  & =-5t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535764 true] [17592186134483 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535764 true] [17592186134483 1100 "Let $V = C[0, 1]$, the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[0, 1]$. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$⟨x(t), y(t)⟩ = ∫_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)dt$,\nfind the orthogonal projection of $f(t) = 2t^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by $g(t) = 6t - 3$." 13194139535764 false] [17592186134483 1100 "Let $V=C[0,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[0,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $f(t)=2{t}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by $g(t)=6t-3.$" 13194139535764 true] [17592186134483 1145 "The orthogonal projection of $f(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{g(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t)=\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),g(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{t}^{2}\\cdot (6t-3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(12{t}^{3}-6{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[3{t}^{4}-2{t}^{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(3-2)-0 \\\\  & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),g(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6t-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{t}^{2}-36t+9)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[12{t}^{3}-18{t}^{2}+9t]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(12-18+9)-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (6t-3) \\\\  & =2t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365165 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365166 13194139535764 true] [17592186365165 1089 "q-104927" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365165 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535764 true] [17592186365165 1100 "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $2$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $p(t)={t}^{2}+3t-2$ onto the subspace spanned by $q(t)=2t-2.$" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365165 1113 #uuid "36779e87-7605-5095-bb25-fa2df5619013" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365165 1145 "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{q(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)=\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}\\,+\\,3t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,+\\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,3t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\,+\\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,3t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot (2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =16+4 \\\\  & =20,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),q(t)⟩ & =q(-1)q(-1)+q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,+(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\,+(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =16+4+0 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{20}\\cdot (2t-2) \\\\  & =2t-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365167 13194139535764 true] [17592186365166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365168 13194139535764 true] [17592186365166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365169 13194139535764 true] [17592186365166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365170 13194139535764 true] [17592186365166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365171 13194139535764 true] [17592186365166 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535764 true] [17592186365166 1041 "selection" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365166 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365167 13194139535764 true] [17592186365166 1110 #uuid "af11f1e1-dbb3-5edd-b401-15dd37d6c964" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365167 1034 "2t-2" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365167 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535764 true] [17592186365167 1111 #uuid "c0fc551e-2e2c-5b7b-a0db-f4a834e6e687" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365168 1034 "2-2t" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535764 true] [17592186365168 1111 #uuid "6c97060c-5797-5ba2-a9c6-a3c5dfb80565" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365169 1034 "4-2t" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535764 true] [17592186365169 1111 #uuid "b445e306-35e7-59bd-b34a-2e1dd542366e" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365170 1034 "4-4t" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535764 true] [17592186365170 1111 #uuid "a11abc27-5080-5fcc-bd3e-d58e027e4b4c" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365171 1034 "4t-4" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365171 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535764 true] [17592186365171 1111 #uuid "3b81837e-d514-5381-a4a5-9da5c5ced503" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365172 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365173 13194139535764 true] [17592186365172 1089 "q-104936" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365172 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535764 true] [17592186365172 1100 "Let $V=C[-1,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[-1,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $f(t)={t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}+2$ onto the subspace spanned by $g(t)=5{t}^{2}+1.$" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365172 1113 #uuid "4a15e7fe-ea3e-5b2e-bcc2-2e4f7497493e" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365172 1145 "The orthogonal projection of $f(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{g(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t)=\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),g(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}+2)\\cdot (5{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(5{t}^{5}+50{t}^{4}+{t}^{3}+20{t}^{2}+2)\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{5}{6}{t}^{6}+10{t}^{5}+\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{4}+\\frac{20}{3}{t}^{3}+2t]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{6}+10+\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{20}{3}+2)-(\\frac{5}{6}-10+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{20}{3}-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{112}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),g(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(5{t}^{2}+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(25{t}^{4}+10{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[5{t}^{5}+\\frac{10}{3}{t}^{3}+t]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(5+\\frac{10}{3}+1)-(-5-\\frac{10}{3}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{112}{3})}{(\\frac{56}{3})}\\cdot (5{t}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =2(5{t}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =10{t}^{2}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365174 13194139535764 true] [17592186365173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365175 13194139535764 true] [17592186365173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365176 13194139535764 true] [17592186365173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365177 13194139535764 true] [17592186365173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365178 13194139535764 true] [17592186365173 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535764 true] [17592186365173 1041 "selection" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365173 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365175 13194139535764 true] [17592186365173 1110 #uuid "7ac5d6b5-53c6-5ba2-a77b-e4b63d9f3cc5" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365174 1034 "-5{t}^{2}+2" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535764 true] [17592186365174 1111 #uuid "bf4bea6d-2e30-52e5-98e7-edf4e55f676a" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365175 1034 "10{t}^{2}+2" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535764 true] [17592186365175 1111 #uuid "e5f12df4-cc65-5436-a026-cff66d1f218c" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365176 1034 "-{t}^{2}+2" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535764 true] [17592186365176 1111 #uuid "f1d3a344-c8f5-5ce9-adef-0e806fe360da" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365177 1034 "5{t}^{2}+1" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365177 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535764 true] [17592186365177 1111 #uuid "4160c9de-5b36-54e8-8e64-f5625de91ecc" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365178 1034 "5{t}^{2}+2" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365178 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535764 true] [17592186365178 1111 #uuid "869904bb-d61b-50d8-b430-2b803f29a800" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365179 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365180 13194139535764 true] [17592186365179 1089 "q-105186" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365179 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535764 true] [17592186365179 1100 "Let $V=C[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the vector space of continuous functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$, and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=2,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,g(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+6\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t)}$ equals $6.$" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365179 1113 #uuid "e2080217-de30-5eca-8115-9c201cc1f5f5" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365179 1145 "Since the set ${{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)=6,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{2}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t)=\\frac{⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}{⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}\\,{f}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(t){f}_{2}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+6)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t-2{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+6{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ is an odd function, while $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is even. Hence, their product $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ must be an odd function. Now, since we have integrals over the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ which is symmetric about the origin, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩ & =-2{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t) & =\\frac{-2{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t}{⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =\\frac{-2{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t}{{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =6-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535764 true] [17592186365180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365181 13194139535764 true] [17592186365180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365182 13194139535764 true] [17592186365180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365183 13194139535764 true] [17592186365180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365184 13194139535764 t